# Asset objects

Store each reusable clip as a **visual object**:

```json
{
  "id": "visual_door_mist_001",
  "file": "assets/doorways/door_mist_001.mp4",
  "duration": 9.8,
  "width": 1280,
  "height": 720,
  "fps": 25,
  "loop_quality": "good",
  "motion": "slow_forward",
  "brightness": "dark",
  "visual_density": "low",
  "symbols": [
    "threshold",
    "entry",
    "transition",
    "unknown"
  ],
  "moods": [
    "liminal",
    "quiet",
    "mysterious"
  ],
  "tradition_affinity": [
    "corbin",
    "sufism",
    "neoplatonism"
  ],
  "safe_duration": {
    "minimum": 5,
    "maximum": 24
  },
  "filter_compatibility": [
    "blue_night",
    "golden_imaginal",
    "monochrome",
    "tibetan_red"
  ],
  "description": "First-person movement toward a stone doorway appearing through pale mist."
}
```

The model does not need to inspect the pixels every time. It chooses from the metadata.

