# Don’t ask the LLM to choose exact filters

Give it named presets instead:

```json
{
  "treatment": "golden_imaginal"
}
```

Your preset registry decides what that means:

```yaml
golden_imaginal:
  brightness: -0.03
  contrast: 1.08
  saturation: 0.82
  temperature: warm
  vignette: 0.16
  grain: 0.025
  black_floor: 0.04

tibetan_red:
  brightness: -0.05
  contrast: 1.12
  saturation: 0.90
  shadow_tint: deep_red
  highlight_tint: warm_ivory
  grain: 0.035

corbin_blue:
  brightness: -0.06
  contrast: 1.10
  saturation: 0.74
  shadow_tint: midnight_blue
  highlight_tint: pale_gold
  vignette: 0.20

engraving_crisp:
  saturation: 0
  contrast: 1.16
  sharpness: mild
  paper_white: warm
```

This gives thematic variation while protecting the channel identity.

